\f2\i \cf2 What the tax?
\f1\i0  Gerry could not compute the circumstances; without urgency, he did as he was bid. The PAPER agent remained standing behind the desk to Gerry\'92s side.\
The other figure crumpled into a visitor\'92s chair and presented his teeth. Gerry guessed it was a smile. He\'92d never seen such a thing in all the broadcasts as this man trying to smile. Gerry was unsure whether the smile\'92s intent was for reassurance or for inducing terror.\
In a brief flash before anyone present felt compelled to speak, Gerry decided that, now he had met Piotr Dunhilton, CEO of Ulyssia, in the flesh, descriptions of him as a potato face were quite egregious, quite egregious indeed, to potatoes everywhere. The CEO\'92s complexion was more as if the starch from a whole field of potatoes had been extracted, concentrated and compacted into the CEO\'92s pallid face. His eyes appeared as nothing more than God\'92s afterthoughts\'97decorations between the vast forehead under the preternaturally smooth bald head, and the nostrils of his almost non-existent nose. Chalky uniform pegs of teeth were bounded by an awkward career-criminal smile which was in turn delimited by lips no more generous than a technical stroke of a 2-H pencil on a draughtsman\'92s board.\
\'91I understand people in these halls call you Very Hard Man,\'92 the compacted potato said, now thankfully lacking the attempt at a smile.\
\'91I, ah, prefer 
\f2\i Gerry
\f1\i0 , your Serene Corporateness.\'92\
\'91Oh?\'92 the CEO said as if playing vaudeville. \'91Well, I was informed,\'92 he said, glancing at the standing man, \'91you, 
\f2\i Gerry,
\f1\i0  are exactly the stuff we\'92re looking for in these troubling times.\'92\
\'91Sir?\'92\
\'91The previous Commissioner of Police has somewhat unexpectedly and suddenly retired,\'92 the CEO said. \
\'91I thought he was on holiday,\'92 Gerry jabbered.\
\'91Well, retirement 
\f2\i is
\f1\i0  the most final of holidays.\'92\
Gerry nodded. \'91I imagine, while on holiday he retired from a window?\'92 Falling from a window was the state\'92s preferred method of induced retirement.\
\'91Ah, no.\'92 Dunhilton prevaricated. \'91It seems someone wanted to send us a ghastlier message.\'92\
What could be more ghastly than a window-related retirement? Depending on the weather, the retiree could experience both the caustic effects of the Layer eating their flesh and bones, and the sudden splat as they hit the ground. For some, the brief plummet was their first and last trip below the Layer.\
The CEO stood, and Gerry aped likewise. The CEO offered his hand and Gerry autonomically clasped it. The CEO shook and said, \'91Congratulations. Special Agent Jones here will read you in. Good day.\'92\
The CEO left while Gerry stammered. Agent Jones ground his teeth.\
